Feature: Compiled skill layout

  Background:
    Given a fixture repository

  # Compiled skill layout 1
  Scenario Outline: Compiled skill layout 1 writes frontmatter, marker, body and file sections in order
    Given the file skills/engineering/alpha/SKILL.md has content <skill>
    And the file skills/engineering/alpha/notes.md has content <notes>
    And the file skills/engineering/alpha/scripts/run.sh has content <script>
    And the file skills/engineering/alpha/agents/openai.yaml has content <yaml>
    When I run compile-skills
    Then the exit code is 0
    And the file compiled/alpha.md is exactly <compiled>

    Examples:
      | skill | notes | script | yaml | compiled |
      | ---\nname: alpha\ndescription: Alpha fixture.\n---\n\n# Alpha\n\nSee [notes](notes.md).\n\n | # Notes\n\nBack to [the skill](./SKILL.md).\n | echo hi\n | interface:\n  display_name: "Alpha"\n | ---\nname: alpha\ndescription: Alpha fixture.\n---\n\n<!-- Generated by bb compile-skills from skills/engineering/alpha/. Do not edit. -->\n\n# Skill: alpha\n\n# Alpha\n\nSee [notes](#file-alphanotesmd).\n\n## File: alpha/notes.md\n\n# Notes\n\nBack to [the skill](#skill-alpha).\n\n## File: alpha/scripts/run.sh\n\n```sh\necho hi\n```\n |

  # Compiled skill layout 2
  Scenario Outline: Compiled skill layout 2 keeps the frontmatter verbatim
    Given the file skills/<bucket>/alpha/SKILL.md has content <skill>
    When I run compile-skills
    Then the file compiled/alpha.md includes <frontmatter>
    And the file compiled/alpha.md includes <marker>

    Examples:
      | bucket      | skill | frontmatter | marker |
      | in-progress | ---\nname: alpha\ndescription: Alpha.\ndisable-model-invocation: true\nargument-hint: <topic>\n---\n\n# Alpha\n | ---\nname: alpha\ndescription: Alpha.\ndisable-model-invocation: true\nargument-hint: <topic>\n---\n\n<!-- | <!-- Generated by bb compile-skills from skills/in-progress/alpha/. Do not edit. -->\n\n# Skill: alpha\n\n# Alpha\n |

  # Compiled skill layout 3
  Scenario Outline: Compiled skill layout 3 fences non-Markdown files by extension and backtick length
    Given a skill alpha in bucket engineering
    And the file skills/engineering/alpha/<path> has content <content>
    When I run compile-skills
    Then the file compiled/alpha.md includes <section>

    Examples:
      | path             | content            | section |
      | template.sh      | set -e\n           | ## File: alpha/template.sh\n\n```sh\nset -e\n``` |
      | config.cjs       | module.exports = {};\n | ## File: alpha/config.cjs\n\n```cjs\nmodule.exports = {};\n``` |
      | snippet.txt      | a\n```\nb\n        | ## File: alpha/snippet.txt\n\n````txt\na\n```\nb\n```` |
      | Makefile         | all:\n             | ## File: alpha/Makefile\n\n```\nall:\n``` |

  # Compiled skill layout 4
  Scenario Outline: Compiled skill layout 4 sorts file sections by path and leaves out agents/openai.yaml
    Given a skill alpha in bucket engineering
    And the file skills/engineering/alpha/<first> has content first\n
    And the file skills/engineering/alpha/<second> has content second\n
    When I run compile-skills
    Then in the file compiled/alpha.md, <first_heading> comes before <second_heading>
    And the file compiled/alpha.md has 0 occurrences of <excluded>

    Examples:
      | first     | second     | first_heading         | second_heading         | excluded         |
      | B.md      | a.md       | ## File: alpha/B.md   | ## File: alpha/a.md    | agents/openai.yaml |
      | docs/x.md | notes.md   | ## File: alpha/docs/x.md | ## File: alpha/notes.md | display_name |
